Z||000009||FLASHY||11-05-2001||05:27 PM||||Ok, I tried searching by a username but I want to sort it by date (eg. most recent post made by *******) rather than look through the date on every find. They don't seem to be in chronological order. Am I missing something?||||reg||1
Z||000010||Cliff Pennock||11-05-2001||05:55 PM||||That's because they are always sorted by relevance. A higher date doesn't make a post more relevant. I'm not sure why sorting by date is important, but I'll see how much work it is to implement such a thing.||||reg||1
Z||000011||FLASHY||11-05-2001||06:19 PM||||It's kind of confusing to explain but here it goes...<P>I'll remember the person's name who said something interesting within the last few days but can't remember which topic it was in. (There are times when replies start to get distant from the original topic so it gets confusing where I read it). So I'll search for that person's name and then check their posts within the last few days.<P>The other time I needed the search results to be in chronological order (probably more important than my first example) is when I search a broad word such as "scoops" but wanted to find the most recent replies on that subject. It takes a while to scroll down all the results to find the dates that are the most recent.<P>I hope that all made sense.||||reg||1
Z||000012||DRH||11-05-2001||06:31 PM||||Cliff,<P>I just posted the date sort question in Announcements. <P>The relevance sort is GREAT (a definite improvement) when I am just looking for info on a subject. The date would help when I already have a particular thread in mind.<P>If you can't change it I'll just use the time I saved on the search scrolling through a couple of pages.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><BR>Edit to add:<BR>Date sort would also be nice if I'm just trying to catch up on the latest info on a particular subject.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by DRH (edited 11-05-2001).]||||reg||1
